.TH FILE_READ 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
file_read \- read bytes from a descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B long file_read(long descriptor, char* buffer, long byte_count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads bytes into a writable buffer. Reads may be short and are not retried.
Supply a nonnegative byte count and sufficient buffer space.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes read, zero at EOF, or \-1 with errno set.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR file_open (3crunch),
.BR read (3crunch)
